#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""layer-build -- put the packages a base container is missing into ONE SquashFS layer.

    layer-build --base <pinned.sif> --env <environment.yml|conda-env-export.json> --id <name>

Read MANUAL.md for the contract, the conflict rules and the exit codes; `--help` for the flags.

The split in this file is deliberate, and it is the whole design:

  * the middle is pure: parse the environment, compare it with what the image already has, decide
    the plan. No I/O, no subprocess, no clock. That is what the tests exercise, and it is what makes
    "fail loudly on a conflict" a rule you can read rather than a behaviour you have to trust.
  * the edges do I/O: singularity, mksquashfs, the filesystem, one function each, each failing
    loudly instead of guessing.
"""


